WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.868
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 4, Network security, which is 14 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.659
This lesson covers objective 4 point 3.

00:00:10.659 --> 00:00:16.742
Given a scenario, apply network security features, defense techniques, and solutions.

00:00:16.742 --> 00:00:21.680
Today's concept: what DNSSEC actually protects, and what it does not.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.600
Here a client looks up a name from a zone that is validly signed.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.974
The answer comes back with a signature.

00:00:29.974 --> 00:00:36.370
The client checks the chain of trust, and it can be sure the data came from the right zone and was not changed on the way.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.555
But look at the question itself.

00:00:38.555 --> 00:00:40.295
It still travels in the clear.

00:00:40.295 --> 00:00:42.440
Anyone watching the wire can read it.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.771
So an analyst who says the lookup is now hidden needs a correction.

00:00:46.771 --> 00:00:49.041
DNSSEC validates origin and integrity.

00:00:49.041 --> 00:00:51.370
Confidentiality is a different problem.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.869
On the exam, when you see DNSSEC, think origin and integrity.

00:00:57.869 --> 00:01:04.993
If the question asks about hiding the lookup, that needs a separate mechanism like DNS over HTTPS or TLS.

00:01:04.993 --> 00:01:07.300
That's objective four point three.
